  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reducing barriers and Increasing Demands for Reproductive Health Services in Ethiopia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To increase demand for and use of quality, acceptable reproductive health services by poor and excluded communities, specifically prevention of unintended pregnancies and assurance of safe pregnancy and childbirth. These changes will be measured by using indicators on: Contraceptive Prevalence Rates (CPR); Contraceptive Acceptance Rates (CAR); proportion of births delivered by a skilled birth attendant; and teenage pregnancy rates.</narrative>
  </description>
